Mastering AWS Lambda: Go Serverless!
Topic: Run Code Without Managing Servers with AWS Lambda

As part of my hashtag#AWSChallenge, I explored AWS Lambda, a core serverless compute service that lets you run backend logic or microservices code with zero infrastructure management.

💡 What is AWS Lambda?
AWS Lambda lets you run code on demand in response to events like:

API Gateway calls

S3 uploads

DynamoDB stream changes

Scheduled (cron) jobs

CloudWatch Alarms, SNS, EventBridge, and more

⚙️ Lambda Basics
✅ Languages Supported: Python, Node.js, Java, Go, .NET, Ruby
✅ Triggers: API Gateway, S3, DynamoDB, EventBridge, CloudWatch, SNS
✅ Execution Time: Max 15 mins
✅ Memory: 128MB to 10GB
✅ Free Tier: 1M free requests per month (awesome for startups 🚀)

🧠 Use Case
🚀 Serverless REST API using Lambda + API Gateway
📦 Image processing pipeline with S3 + Lambda
🧾 Automated invoice processing with S3 + Textract + Lambda
🔄 Real-time data processing with DynamoDB Streams + Lambda
⏰ Scheduled cleanup tasks using EventBridge cron + Lambda

🛠️ DevOps Friendly
Create & deploy using AWS Console, CLI, SAM, or Terraform

Monitor logs via CloudWatch

Versioning & Aliases for safe deployment

Easily integrated into CI/CD pipelines

🔐 Bonus: Security Best Practices
✅ Use least privilege IAM roles
✅ Store secrets in AWS Secrets Manager or SSM Parameter Store
✅ Use Environment Variables securely
